 saying wait a second why  is it that Democratic politicians are  fed by unions who benefit from public  taxpayer dollars so there is a  connection here and there's corruption  in this whole system in my opinion but  Republicans are the ones who because  they are negatively affected by it are  jumping up and screaming bloody murder  last question what do you see happening  the next five years are you optimistic  where's it going to break what's  happening oh I I'm optimistic and I you  know what I believe that if you have an  honest discussion of this it's just so  overwhelming we just look at the numbers  you look right now there's that scandal  in Atlanta and elsewhere over test  scores being faked you look at the  dropout rate in this country how many  children are not getting out of high  school at a time of global economic  competition competition for jobs nine  percent unemployment how can you say to  so many young people  so you don't need a high school  education we're not going to give you  the opportunity to make us something to  make something of yourself in America I  think it's a condemnation of America and  I think that it's contrary to the  American spirit so no I I tend to be  very optimistic that this is a breakout  issue that we're on the verge of us what  I call or described to you earlier as  this these civil rights issue the  political issue of the 21st century  thank you very much with one Williams  I'm Matt Welch for reason TV
 

